  "finalText": "RCSB PDB has **10 entries** with a protein entity mapped to human leptin.\n\n1. **Accession:** UniProtKB search (`gene_exact:LEP AND organism_id:9606 AND reviewed:true`) returned one reviewed entry, **P41159** (Leptin, gene LEP, *Homo sapiens*).\n2. **PDB search:** I queried the RCSB Search API for released entries where `rcsb_polymer_entity_container_identifiers.reference_sequence_identifiers.database_accession` exactly equals `P41159` and `database_name` equals `UniProt`, returning entries with all hits. It reported `total_count: 10`:\n\n1AX8, 7Z3Q, 8AVE, 8AVF, 8AVO, 8K6Z, 8X80, 8X81, 8X85, 9PUO\n\nThe query used two separate conditions rather than one combined condition, so in principle they could have matched different references within an entry. That has no effect here, because P41159 is a UniProt accession and can only match a UniProt reference. The list covers released entries only, as of today's search.\n\nANSWER: 10 | 1AX8, 7Z3Q, 8AVE, 8AVF, 8AVO, 8K6Z, 8X80, 8X81, 8X85, 9PUO"
